20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.8 ⛲  gemini-3.5 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.112 211.9KB 13.91s
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #Thank you for sharing the updated workspace files for nitrologic Relay (v1.8.8).
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #Based on the source files and documentation provided, here is an analysis of how the components of
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #your research tool are structured and how they align with your roadmap:
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #Architecture Overview
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #1. `relay.ts` (Core CLI & Model Router):
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #   * Acts as the central hub, managing multi-provider API connections (OpenAI, DeepSeek, Google
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #Gemini, and Anthropic Claude).
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #   * Implements custom session management, file sharing/commit flows, and tool calling
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #(`read_time`, `submit_file`, `fetch_file`, `tag_slop`).
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #   * Contains robust local speech-generation integrations, including a custom WAV header packager
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #for Gemini's PCM output, as well as support for macOS native `say` and OpenAI TTS.
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #   * Runs a TCP server on port 8081 to communicate with external bots.
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c32 [gemini-3.5] #2. `slopprompt.ts` (Raw Mode Terminal Multiplexer):
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #   * Puts the terminal into raw mode to handle interactive user input, custom history navigation,
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #and shortcode parsing (e.g., `:parrot:` to emoji).
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #   * Calculates visual character widths accurately using custom grapheme segmentation and
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #double-width checks to prevent terminal layout distortion.
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #   * Uses non-blocking multiplexing (`Promise.race`) to handle stdin input and TCP bot traffic
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #concurrently without blocking the terminal.
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #3. `slopbot.ts` (Discord Bridge):
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #   * Connects to the local TCP port 8081.
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #   * Bridges Discord message creation and mentions directly into the Relay session, and chunks long
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #model responses to fit within Discord's 2000-character limit.
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #Roadmap & Next Steps
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #Based on your planning notes and the shared Exa Search API documentation, here are some
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #areas we can explore or implement next:
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #• Websearch Integration (Exa / Neural Search):
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #  * You have included the `exa-js` SDK documentation. We can design a clean integration for a web
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #search tool within `relay.ts` that respects your `config.search` flag.
20e59c33 [gemini-3.5] #  * This can be set up as a system-level tool call or routed through specific models that support
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #tool-use billing and account hints.
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #• Project Support (`relay.md` and `relay.log`):
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #  * Refining the transition when a project is activated via `/project`, ensuring the current
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #workspace paths are restored and the `relay.log` file is safely appended.
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #• Sloppybots Discord Testing:
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #  * Addressing any stability or event-handling details within `slopbot.ts` for active Discord
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #channels.
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #Please let me know how you would like to proceed, or if you would like to begin drafting the
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #integration for the Exa search tool!
20e59c34 [gemini-3.5] #
