22356668 [claude-sonnet-5] # ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.068 205.8KB 27.15s
22356668 [claude-sonnet-5] #Thanks for sharing the whole Relay project — this is all new to me. A few observations:
22356668 [claude-sonnet-5] #
22356668 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Version mismatch*: README.md says `1.9.3` but `relay.ts` defines `relayVersion="1.9.4"`.
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #Might be worth syncing those, or is `forge.md`/`README.md` deliberately a version behind?
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Overall architecture*: This is a substantial multi-provider LLM CLI — a single
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #abstraction layer (`connectAccount`) dispatching to `connectOpenAI`, `connectDeepSeek`,
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #`connectGoogle`, `connectAnthropic`, each normalizing responses into a common `{choices, usage}`
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #shape so `relay()` can treat them uniformly. Handling three very different tool-calling conventions
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #(OpenAI's `tool_calls`, Gemini's `functionCalls()`, Anthropic's `tool_use` content blocks) in one
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #place is a good design call — keeps the core chat loop provider-agnostic.
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Terminal handling*: `slopprompt.ts`'s raw-mode reader with grapheme segmentation, custom
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #wide-character tables (`isDoubleWidth`, `discordWide`/`discordThin`/`discordThick`), and shortcode
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #expansion (`:heart:` etc.) is a lot of careful work for something that usually gets glossed over.
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #The separate Discord-width vs terminal-width logic implies you've hit real rendering mismatches
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #between console fonts and Discord's emoji metrics.
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Project/share model*: The `roha.keyedShares[key]` / `roha.keyedProjects[key]` scheme tied
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #to folder name via a shared `relay.md` sentinel file is a neat way to get per-project context
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #persistence without an explicit project file format — dropping a `relay.md` into a directory to key
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #a project is a nice discoverability trick.
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Cost tracking*: `bumpModel()` computing spend from `modelSpecs[model].pricing` and
22356669 [claude-sonnet-5] #decrementing `roha.lode[account].credit` gives you live budget tracking per account — that plus the
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #`/dump` and `/account` commands suggests this doubles as a cost-auditing tool across providers, not
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #just a chat client.
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #• One possible rough edge*: in `relay.ts`, `resetModel()` throws away `mut.errors`/state a
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #bit implicitly, and `nextActiveModel()` walks `modelList` by index rather than filtering first —
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #with a large model list this is fine, just wanted to flag it in case cycling through
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #inactive/hidden models is a common pain point.
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #If you want, I can dig into a specific piece — the Gemini/Anthropic normalization code, the ANSI
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #markdown renderer (`mdToAnsi`), or the websearch provider notes in the README — just point me at
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #what's most useful right now.
2235666a [claude-sonnet-5] #
